\begin_layout Problem
This is a two-person dynamic game of perfect information that is played
 as follows.
 There is a 
\begin_inset Formula $K\times K$
\end_inset

 grid of points 
\begin_inset Formula $X$
\end_inset

 where 
\begin_inset Formula $K\geq2$
\end_inset

.
 The points in the grid are numbered in matrix fashin, so that 
\begin_inset Formula $x_{11}$
\end_inset

 is the upper left corner and 
\begin_inset Formula $x_{KK}$
\end_inset

 is the lower right corner.
 Player 1 begins by taking the first chomp (bite) out of the grid.
 Specifically, he selects a point in the grid 
\begin_inset Formula $x_{kl}\in X$
\end_inset

, and removes it along with all the points above and to the left of it (i.e.,
 all pont 
\begin_inset Formula $x_{ij}\in X$
\end_inset

 with 
\begin_inset Formula $i\leq k$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $j\leq l$
\end_inset

).
 Player two then moves, taking the next chomp out of the remaining point
 in the grid, and so on.
 The lose is the player who takes the last chomp (i.e., the one who chomps
 point 
\begin_inset Formula $x_{KK}$
\end_inset

).
\end_layout

